## --help
rc=0
grove.backup.get — read the grove backup

usage:
  rhx grove.backup.get                          this box's last run, as one line
  rhx grove.backup.get --list                   every grove the bucket holds, latest backup each
  rhx grove.backup.get --from <grove> --list    every unit that grove left, with date and class

options:
  --list            list, rather than read this box's status
  --from <grove>    the grove whose units to list (implies --list)

exit:
  0  the read completed — a ✗ FAILED or ✗ STALE status included: the verdict is the line, not the exit
  1  the bucket gave no answer; a retry may cure it
  2  a constraint: bad args, a credential or grant, no such grove

to restore a unit:  rhx grove.backup.restore --help
on a grove, run each from this repo's checkout: cd ~/git/more/dev-env-setup

